Maximus runs third-party software and models on your computer. They are not
part of this source tree and keep their own licenses:

- llama.cpp / llama-server (MIT) — runs the language model locally.
- Node.js (MIT) — runs the local server.
- Tauri (Apache-2.0 / MIT) — the desktop shell.
- whisper.cpp (MIT) and KB-Whisper models (Apache-2.0) — speech to text.
- Language models such as Google Gemma (Gemma Terms of Use), Qwen
  (Apache-2.0), Llama (Llama Community License) and Mistral (Apache-2.0) are
  downloaded on first use. Their licenses are shown in the app before download.
- Optional cloud model providers (Berget AI, OpenAI, Anthropic, Google,
  OpenRouter) are used only if you turn them on, under their own terms.
